# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# tsai-portal — PRODUCTION environment (Cloud Run)
#
# Next.js loads this for `next build` / `next start` when NODE_ENV=production,
# and the standalone server loads it at runtime. This file is the SINGLE tracked
# source of non-secret production configuration:
#
#   • Non-secret prod values are SET here (they are the defaults baked into the
#     image — the app stays correctly configured even if Cloud Run env drifts).
#   • SECRETS are NEVER set here (this file is tracked in git). They are injected
#     by Cloud Run at runtime (Terraform env blocks / Secret Manager) and listed
#     below, commented, as the completeness contract.
#   • Cloud Run env vars and Docker build args OVERRIDE this file (process env has
#     higher precedence than env files).
#
# `.env.local` is the DEV counterpart: gitignored, never enters the Docker build
# context, always wins locally.
#
# When you add a var to .env.local, add it here in the same commit — set if
# non-secret, commented if platform-injected. A var that exists in dev and is
# silently absent in production is the failure this file guards against.
#
# Added 2026-08-27. Until then portal had NEITHER file, so `bifrost release`
# could not resolve the anon key and refused to build it — the only product of
# the three without an env contract.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Non-secret production values -------------------------------------------

# DGX backend origin (Tailscale Funnel) — the S2 data plane.
TSAI_DGX_ORIGIN=https://spark-62db.tail18f71b.ts.net:8443

# Supabase public origin. The browser resolves same-origin /supabase on Cloud
# Run; server-side calls and build-time inlining use this value.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://spark-62db.tail18f71b.ts.net:8443/supabase

# Gateway fronting hockey-api.
API_GATEWAY_URL=https://spark-62db.tail18f71b.ts.net:8443

# --- PLATFORM-INJECTED SECRETS (Cloud Run env / Secret Manager) --------------
#
# Listed, never set. Portal's source reads each of these; if one is missing at
# runtime the page that needs it fails, and this list is how you find out which.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=   # public by design (inlined in the browser
#                                  # bundle) but still resolved at build time —
#                                  # `bifrost release` reads it from the env or
#                                  # the reset-proof vault, never from git.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=       # bypasses RLS. Never in a repo.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

# --- PLATFORM-INJECTED (non-secret, environment-specific) --------------------
#
# TSAI_DEPLOY_TARGET=              # selects topology at build time (rewrites);
#                                  # owned by the Dockerfile builder stage and the
#                                  # Cloud Run service env, so a local
#                                  # `next build` stays local.
# PORT=                            # supplied by Cloud Run.
